{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The preamble makes Wells Fargo Bank, N.A. the Auction Agent acting \"not in its individual capacity but solely as agent of WELLS FARGO BANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION (the 'Tmstee')\" — the same entity as its own principal, and the defined term is misspelled. A court could be asked which capacity binds and whether the agency limitation has content when principal and agent are one person.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24},
     {"issue": "The preamble names the Company as a contracting party, but Section 5.5 confines enforcement rights to the Auction Agent, the Bond Insurer and BD. Whether the Company is a party with rights is a genuine cross-provision question.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.3}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The recital defines the four series collectively as the \"Series 2004 Bonds\" and then says the same instruments are \"sometimes referred to together herein as the 'Series 2004 Auction Bonds'\", creating two labels for one set without a rule for when each applies. The word \"sometimes\" leaves the boundary between the two defined terms undrawn.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27},
     {"issue": "Section 1.3(f) treats \"Series 2004 Bonds\" and \"Series 2004 Auction Bonds\" as distinct referents to which any reference to \"Bonds\" applies, which sits awkwardly with this recital's equation of the two. Reconciling the recital with 1.3(f) is a real interpretive step.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The recital says only that BD \"is to perform certain duties set forth herein\" without identifying them, so it adds nothing a court could measure. Its vagueness is of the kind courts ignore rather than construe.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.14},
